      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Matrix",
      "problem": "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3-2\\text{i} & 4\\text{i} \\\\ -1-3\\text{i} & 5 & 3-5\\text{i} \\\\ 2+\\text{i} & -5-\\text{i} & -3+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$ What is the value of ${b}_{31}+{b}_{32}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3-2\\text{i} & 4\\text{i} \\\\ -1-3\\text{i} & 5 & 3-5\\text{i} \\\\ 2+\\text{i} & -5-\\text{i} & -3+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-4} & \\overset{―}{3-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{4\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-1-3\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{5} & \\overset{―}{3-5\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{2+\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-5-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-3+3\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3+2\\text{i} & -4\\text{i} \\\\ -1+3\\text{i} & 5 & 3+5\\text{i} \\\\ 2-\\text{i} & -5+\\text{i} & -3-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{31}+{b}_{32}=(2-\\text{i})+(-5+\\text{i})=-3.$",
